# Rust build output. `target/` rather than `/target` on purpose: rust-analyzer's flycheck
# writes one next to whatever Cargo.toml it was last pointed at, which after a move is a
# directory that no longer belongs to the project.
target/
*.pdb
*.rs.bk

# What scripts/release.ps1 writes: the setup .exe and the update feed.
dist

# Logs and crash dumps
logs
*.log
*.dmp

# What the diagnostic flags write when run from the repo root: `--probe out.png`,
# `--probe-settings out.png`, `scripts/shot.ps1 -Out settings.png`. Root-anchored, so the
# artwork under design/, docs/media/ and website/assets/ is untouched.
/*.png
/*.exe

# Secrets. `.env.example` is committed on purpose and must not be matched here.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.local

# Editor, OS and tooling droppings
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Assistant / editor tooling — local to whoever is working, not part of the project.
# The skills under .claude/skills/ are the exception and are committed.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
.cursor/
.codex-video-review/
.codex-video-review-current/
.openai/
.agents/
.agent/

# Local / one-off artifacts (keep the repo lean)
*_errors.txt
tsc_output.txt
clean_log.txt
temp*.txt
temp_*.txt
patch_*.js
*_patch.js
apply_*.js
surgical_patch.js

# archive/electron/ — the retired 1.x build. Nothing there is built any more, but these rules
# keep a checkout clean for anyone who opens it and runs `npm install`.
#
# Every one of them is anchored to that folder. They were written when that tree was the repo
# root, and a bare basename like `release` matches at every level — which is how an unanchored
# copy of this list quietly ignored .claude/skills/release.
node_modules
node_modules.onedrive-*/
dist-ssr
archive/electron/release/
archive/electron/build-out*
archive/electron/build-out-update-validation/
archive/electron/build/icon.ico
archive/electron/build/appx/
# Compiled from backend/native-helper/rovyl-helper.cs by scripts/build-native-helper.cjs,
# which ran first in `npm run build`/`dist`. csc stamps a fresh MVID every compile, so a
# tracked copy was dirty after every build and the committed bytes were never the shipped ones.
archive/electron/backend/rovyl-helper.exe
archive/electron/resources/bin/rovyl-helper.exe
archive/electron/backend/*.backup
archive/electron/backend/debug_*.json
archive/electron/TODO.html
